---
title: Updating a user
endpoint: /users/{id}
method: patch
---

Use this endpoint to change a teammate's permissions.

You'll need your [primary API key](/api-authentication) and write access to newsletter settings. Other API keys can't change teammates' permissions, even if they have write access to newsletter settings.

You can only give a teammate permissions you have yourself. This also applies when you change your own permissions.

For example, if you only have read access to subscribers, you can't send `subscriber: write`, even if your teammate already has write access. Someone with write access will need to make that change.

Include every permission you want your teammate to keep in the `permissions` object. Any permissions you leave out are set to `none`.

If you use any API key other than your primary API key or include permissions above your own, you'll receive a `403` with the code `permission_denied`. Your teammate's permissions won't change.
